meta {
  name: Get Product Subpaths
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/attributes
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.brand: eq Plytix
}

docs {
  `GET /api/v3/products/{identifier}/{path}` — fetch a single expanded subresource
  of a product. The primary request here runs `/attributes`; see the examples below
  for `/categories`, `/assets`, `/relationships`, and `/static_lists`. Confirmed
  live 2026-09-07/08 against "David's Dev Account".

  ## Confirmed valid subpaths on products
  | Path | Returns | Notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | `/attributes` | Full attributes map as `data` | Same object embedded in a full GET |
  | `/attributes/<name>` | Single attribute value as `data` | e.g. `data: "Plytix"` |
  | `/categories` | Array of expanded `ProductCategoryGetOutputDto` | id, name, parent_id, path, slug, order, n_children, modified |
  | `/assets` | Array of expanded `AssetOutputDto` | id, content_type, checksum, extension, file_size, file_type, filename, path, n_catalogs, n_products, status, created, modified |
  | `/relationships` | Flat array of `{relationship_id, relationship_label, product_id}` | Different (flatter) shape than the `product_relationships` object in a full GET |
  | `/static_lists` | Array of Static product lists this product belongs to | Smart list membership has no product-side trace — see Static Lists example |

  ## Subpath-discovery 400 trick (applies to all v3 resources)
  Hitting `GET /{resource}/{id}/{bogus_path}` with an unrecognised `{path}` returns
  `400 {"errors":[{"name":"ValueError","description":"Field '<path>' not found.
  Available fields: [...]"}]}` listing the resource's raw internal model fields.
  For products: `['id','account_id','sku','label','gtin','status','attributes',
  'thumbnail_id','parent_id','num_variations','product_level','product_family_id',
  'product_family_model_id','overwritten_attributes','mark_as_deleted',
  'product_relationships','created','modified','last_context',
  'modified_user_audit','created_user_audit']`.
  Caveat: this raw list does NOT include computed/joined relations (`categories`,
  `assets`, `relationships`) that are still valid subpaths (all confirmed 200).
  Use this trick early in each new resource phase before guessing subpath names.

  ## Assets subpath spot-check findings
  `GET /assets/{id}/{path}` tested directly against asset id `6a38f5e1c3d65a5f868b18a5`:
  - `/categories` → 200, `[]` (asset not in any category).
  - `/attributes`, `/relationships`, `/products` → all **400** (`ValueError`) —
    assets have no attributes/relationships concept and there is no
    reverse `assets/{id}/products` lookup.

  ## Static lists: Smart list membership has no product-side trace
  `GET /products/{id}/static_lists` reflects only Static list membership. The
  Smart list (`6aa0322d2b6fd055ffb7cabb`) that matches this product via its `sku`
  filter does NOT appear anywhere on the product. The only way to discover Smart
  list membership is to re-execute the list's own `query` against `GET /products`
  — there is no reverse-lookup from the product side for dynamic/Smart lists.

  ## Relationships: two distinct shapes
  The `/relationships` subpath returns a flat `[{relationship_id, relationship_label,
  product_id}]` array — a different (flatter) summary than the nested
  `product_relationships: {<label>: [{quantity, last_modified}]}` object embedded
  in a full `GET /products/{id}`. Neither matches `openapi_pimv3.json`'s
  `relationships` field name. See `Get Product by ID.bru` for context.
}

example {
  name: /attributes - Full Attributes Map
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. The attributes map is returned directly as data (same object embedded under data.attributes on a full GET /products/{id}). Also confirmed: GET /products/{id}/attributes/<name> returns just the single value (e.g. data: "Plytix").

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/attributes
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "brand": "Plytix",
            "color": "Black",
            "amazon_ready": 85.71,
            "basic_information_completeness": 100.0,
            "google_shopping_completeness": 92.86,
            "website_ready": 100.0
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: /categories - Expanded Category Objects
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. Returns fully expanded category objects (not just ids). BAG-10157 has 2 categories — one per taxonomy — each with a path array tracing from root to the category itself.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/categories
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc",
              "name": "Backpacks",
              "parent_id": "6a9f1b402b6fd055ffb7c7da",
              "path": [
                {"id": "6a9f1b3f2b6fd055ffb7c7d9", "name": "Website Taxonomy"},
                {"id": "6a9f1b402b6fd055ffb7c7da", "name": "Bags"},
                {"id": "6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc", "name": "Backpacks"}
              ],
              "slug": "backpacks",
              "order": 0,
              "n_children": 0,
              "modified": "2026-01-15T10:00:00.000000+00:00"
            },
            {
              "id": "6a9f1b542b6fd055ffb7c7dd",
              "name": "Bags & Luggage",
              "parent_id": "6a9f1b532b6fd055ffb7c7dc",
              "path": [
                {"id": "6a9f1b532b6fd055ffb7c7dc", "name": "Google Shopping Taxonomy"},
                {"id": "6a9f1b542b6fd055ffb7c7dd", "name": "Bags & Luggage"}
              ],
              "slug": "bags-luggage",
              "order": 0,
              "n_children": 3,
              "modified": "2026-01-15T10:00:00.000000+00:00"
            }
          ],
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: /assets - Expanded Asset Objects
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. Returns fully expanded AssetOutputDto objects. Asset id 6a38f5e1c3d65a5f868b18a5 is a real read-only fixture in this account.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/assets
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6a38f5e1c3d65a5f868b18a5",
              "content_type": "image/jpeg",
              "checksum": "d41d8cd98f00b204e9800998ecf8427e",
              "extension": "jpg",
              "file_size": 204800,
              "file_type": "Image",
              "filename": "bag-10157-front.jpg",
              "path": "https://assets.plytix.com/6a38f5e1c3d65a5f868b18a5/bag-10157-front.jpg",
              "n_catalogs": 0,
              "n_products": 1,
              "status": "Active",
              "created": "2024-06-01T08:00:00.000000+00:00",
              "modified": "2024-06-01T08:00:00.000000+00:00"
            }
          ],
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: /relationships - Flat Relationship Summary
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. Returns a flat array of {relationship_id, relationship_label, product_id} — different from the nested product_relationships object embedded in GET /products/{id}. relationship_label=related_products confirmed via assertion.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/relationships
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "relationship_id": "6a38f5d6c3d65a5f868b186b",
              "relationship_label": "related_products",
              "product_id": "6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a07"
            }
          ],
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: /static_lists - Static List Membership Only
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-08 (Flow 4). Returns only Static lists this product belongs to. The Smart list (6aa0322d2b6fd055ffb7cabb) that matches this product via its sku filter does NOT appear here — Smart list membership has no product-side trace at all.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4/static_lists
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "6aa025bd2b6fd055ffb7cab4",
              "name": "WC Test Static List",
              "type": "Static",
              "n_products": 1,
              "created": "2026-09-08T14:30:00.000000+00:00",
              "modified": "2026-09-08T14:35:00.000000+00:00"
            }
          ],
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
